# The chip-squeeze check (docs/SPEC.md 11, "World 2's jets"): WinUAE's A500 has about 23 KB less chip RAM free than
# vAmiga's at the same point (Rotor Raider's measurement, 134 -> 111 KB; its unmade BOBs wiped the screen). Ctrl+L, Q at
# the title is the test hook that takes CHIP_SQUEEZE_KB (23) of it away for the run (main.c chipSqueeze).
# World 2 is the biggest chip user (the art block with its set and the jet's copy, the terrain ring made at its load):
# with the squeeze every allocation must still be made (no "AGK ERR out of chip RAM"), the jet BOB drawn from the
# set must show (a jet BOB that was not made would have wiped the frame), and the floor of the game, 64 KB (SPEC 2),
# must hold. Skill 5, ghost: the jets come from the first trip (the first one 10 s into it, W2_JET_FIRST).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 3000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x10
wait 30
expect-serial "AGK chip squeezed"
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 400
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x05
wait 30
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x24
wait 30
press fire 2
wait 60
press up 90
press left 120
wait-serial "jet warn" 1000
wait-serial "jet tell" 600
wait 2
screenshot jettell
wait 60
screenshot after
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR|missing|out of chip"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-min-chip-free 64
